WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.600
If you’re familiar with the SCP Foundation,
then you already know the exact reason why

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.960
there are multiple SCP-001s.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.320
You may even think you know which of them
is the real SCP-001.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.280
But for those of you who are new here, or
who just need a little reminder, the designation

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.640
of “SCP-001” doesn’t refer to a single&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.720
creature, object or entity,&nbsp;
but rather a collection

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.160
of various anomalies that are apparently kept
in containment by the SCP Foundation.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.880
At present, it is unclear why there are multiple
files collected under the shared designation

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.200
of SCP-001.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.280
Some believe it is because these anomalies
are some of the earliest ever contained by

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:43.840
the Foundation.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.560
This would mean that they share the designation
of “SCP-001” as they were likely encountered

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.960
before the SCP Foundation introduced their
current numbering system.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.640
However, there also exists a theory that this
is nothing more than intentional misdirection.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:06.960
Perhaps, the multiple SCP-001 files are an
attempt by the Foundation to conceal information

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.240
about the true SCP-001.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.840
After all, it wouldn’t be the first time
this hyper secretive organization deceived

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:16.480
us.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:22.480
Anomalies sharing the name SCP-001 include
the infamous Scarlet King, the massive Gate

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.800
Guardian, and the world ending event known
as When Day Breaks.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:34.880
But today, we will be using SCP-001 to refer
not to an entity or an event, but to a location.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.880
A location codenamed…

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.640
God’s Blind Spot.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:44.080
Located in an unassuming corner of the world
is a site that the SCP Foundation constructed

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:50.240
and designated as Facility T. According to
their archive, it’s a largely unremarkable

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:56.480
place, situated at a spot on the Sinai Peninsula
- which is a part of Egypt that forms a bridge

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.440
between the continents of Africa and Asia.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:04.240
In the eighteenth century, archaeologists
excavating the area uncovered the remains

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:10.080
of a stone structure, believed to be an inn
that dates back to the second millennium BC.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.320
However, since the construction of Facility&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.560
T, any trace of this structure&nbsp;
has since disappeared.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.840
So, what makes this unremarkable site so important
to the SCP Foundation?

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.640
Why establish a facility if there was nothing
anomalous about its nature?

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:32.480
What distinguishes this SCP-001 site in the
eyes of the Foundation is the area’s profound

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.440
lack of any ambient Akiva radiation.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.920
But what’s Akiva radiation?

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.520
Well, according to the Foundation’s researchers,
it’s a form of cosmic background radiation,

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.040
one that’s not overtly harmful to human
beings.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.000
If you grew up in a strict,&nbsp;
church-going household,&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.760
then it’s highly likely you would have been

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:57.840
exposed to a lot of this non-electromagnetic
radiation and never even realized it.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:03.280
You see, the thing with Akiva radiation is
that it is directly correlated with the amount

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.080
of religious faith a person has.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.600
Regardless of which religion someone follows,
Akiva radiation will form around them.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:17.280
It tends to be harmless to humans, however
certain anomalous entities and SCPs considered

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:22.240
to be demonic in nature can be repelled and
even fought off with high levels of Akiva

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.280
radiation.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.400
The presence of other powerful anomalies,
those considered more benign and even holy,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.840
can also create an increase in this radiation.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:38.080
SCP-001 has earned the nickname “God’s
Blind Spot” for a number of reasons, one

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:43.840
being that it is the only place on Earth with
a natural absence of this Akiva radiation.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.960
The Foundation has conducted experiments that
involved bringing sources known to emit Akiva

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:55.680
radiation into the area of SCP-001, but when
they measured, no change in radiation levels

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:01.600
was detected, meaning that the space around
Facility T does not actively block Akiva radiation

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:07.200
from entering it, but also cannot absorb or
retain this religious radiation.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:13.200
It might be more accurate to say that the
location destroys any trace of residual Akiva,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.520
without damaging the source.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:21.440
A lack of faith-fueled radiation is far from
the only anomalous property of SCP-001 though.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.240
During a number of tests involving D-class
personnel, the Foundation witnessed that,

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:31.600
while in this area, it also becomes impossible
for the death of any human being to occur,

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.280
a discovery that obviously needed to be researched
further.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.760
The first test involved a healthy human male
who was left in a containment cell on the

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.640
SCP-001 site and observed.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:49.040
He had no supplies, no food, no water, yet
over one hundred and twenty days, this man

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.000
stayed alive, never succumbing to starvation
or dehydration.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.360
Next, a female member of D-class was exposed
to a lethal dose of cyanide gas within Facility

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.040
T and suffered none of the expected effects.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.600
Foundation researchers then repeated this
cyanide gas test using thirty common brown

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.640
rats, all of which were killed, proving that
it was only humans that couldn’t be killed

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.440
while within SCP-001.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:21.200
God’s Blind Spot seems to also be able to
slow or halt the effects of terminal illnesses,

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:26.960
as proven when a D-class with stage four cancer
was brought into SCP-001.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.760
Despite her prognosis stating she would be
dead imminently, the woman survived in the

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:34.240
area for almost eight hundred days.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:39.760
Her cancer symptoms never advanced, and she
only died after finally leaving the area of

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.080
SCP-001.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.200
There are limitations to this anomalous effect
though.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.760
One test involved cremating a healthy male
D-class while he was still alive.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:55.120
The man’s body caught fire just as you would
expect it to, and he was burned to death.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.160
According to the findings of that test, and
similar variations, Foundation researchers

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:06.160
have learned that the life preserving qualities
of SCP-001 don’t prevent death by extreme

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.600
external damage.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.960
One of the final tests to take place within
SCP-001 involved a pair of twenty four-year

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.600
old identical D-class twins.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:21.440
One of the twins, designated Twin A, was held
at Facility T, while the other, Twin B, was

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.880
imprisoned in a cell at a different Foundation
site.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:30.960
After observing them for over 26 years, Twin
B aged naturally to the age of fifty.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:36.000
His twin, however, did not appear to age at
all over the course of two and a half decades.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.800
It was only when moved to another facility
that Twin A began to show signs of aging.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:46.640
The aging process for Twin A was rapid too,
and eventually he caught up with his brother.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:51.440
Being a benign, non-threatening anomaly, the
Foundation have been more than happy to use

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.840
God’s Blind Spot to their own advantage.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.160
Facility T was specifically established on
this site to house the headquarters of the

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.120
O5 Council, the overseers of the entire SCP
Foundation.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:07.200
It’s hardly surprising that the overseer
council would want to set up shop here.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.240
After all, it’s the one spot on Planet Earth
where no human being can ever die of natural

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.840
causes, and will not age for the duration
of their stay.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.280
Of course, this locked the O5 Council to one
location, but what if they could replicate

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:24.560
the effects of SCP-001 elsewhere?

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.920
Of course this is what the SCP Foundation
attempted.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:32.560
Following their research into God’s Blind
Spot, the Foundation’s own Doctor Marvin

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:38.480
Scranton attempted to artificially recreate
the area’s anomalous effects somewhere else.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:45.680
His hope was, by generating a vacuum of Akiva
radiation, that a second instance of SCP-001

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:48.480
would occur at a location of his choosing.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.760
Or, as his assistant Bertrand put it, they
planned to build a box and then push God out

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:54.480
of it.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.160
As it turned out, God had other plans.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.440
Doctor Scranton quickly realized the hubris
of his scheme.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:07.200
The Akiva radiation in the selected area rapidly
dropped to zero, just as planned, but then

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.280
something unexpected happened.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.240
Scranton detected an increase in Humes.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.320
These are essentially parts of the fabric
of reality, and are what’s often disrupted

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.960
by reality bending SCPs.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:25.840
Something had come into our world thanks to
the O5 Council’s attempt to recreate SCP-001,

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:31.360
something impossible for the Foundation to
measure or observe.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:37.360
In other words, Scranton had no idea what
he unleashed, or where it went.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:42.960
Following this incident, the O5 Council realized
a worrying increase in the anomalous incidents

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.400
they were encountering.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:49.120
Whether or not this came as a direct result
of their meddling with the fabric of the universe

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:54.480
was unclear, but it forced the Council to
reconsider the focus and direction of the

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.040
entire SCP Foundation.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:02.480
Up until this point, they had been an organization
focused purely on research, but now they had

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.480
to embrace a new approach to how they handled
anomalies.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:11.520
From then on, the Foundation’s objective
became to actively seek out and contain anomalous

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:17.440
entities, creatures, objects, and locations
like SCP-001.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:23.760
Rather than just observing these phenomena
for study, they would Secure, Contain, and

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.720
Protect.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:29.920
The final portion of SCP-001’s file is a
memorandum detailing an arrangement between

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.680
the O5 Council and an unknown “counterparty.”

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.640
In the document, someone named Sheldon Katz
sets out revised terms for the Foundation’s

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.760
continued use of Facility T. Sheldon states
that he has reached an understanding with

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:49.280
the counterparty, and that the contents of
the document are to serve as a formal agreement,

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:54.400
a contract of sorts between the SCP Foundation
and someone else.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:59.200
According to this contract, the incident with
Scranton put a strain on the relationship

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.160
between the Foundation and&nbsp;
whoever the counterparty&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.120
is, and that the O5 Council are seeking to

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:10.960
make amends in order to continue their new
goal of collecting and containing anomalies.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:16.240
So, who was this counterparty that the Overseer
Council was so desperate to appease and have

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.440
on their side?

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:23.600
Who could possibly be a higher power than
the most powerful secret organization on Earth?

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.440
Well, an actual higher power, of course.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:33.760
That’s right, the O5 Council were making
a deal with God, over how they were allowed

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:35.920
to use his Blind Spot.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:40.320
Or at least, a very powerful being that considers
itself to be God.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:44.720
The rules laid out in their agreement stated
that no person was permitted to stay at the

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:51.280
site of SCP-001 for more than a hundred and
twenty years, including members of the O5

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:54.080
Council, along with any&nbsp;
other members of Foundation&nbsp;

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.440
staff, management, researchers, security personnel

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.040
and test subjects.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.920
Additionally, the SCP Foundation’s Ethics
Committee was required to annually report

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.600
any and all of the O5 Council’s decisions
to God.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:12.720
For his own part, God was restricted from
smiting or exacting his terrible wrath upon

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:15.120
any member of Foundation personnel.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:19.600
That’s right, a perk of working for the
SCP Foundation is getting around the clock

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:23.200
divine protection, at least from God himself.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.480
That’s still a lot better than an employee
dental plan.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:32.240
This came with a condition however, that anyone
committing a transgression or mortal sin was

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:37.600
given a ninety day written notice, and an
opportunity to repent their wrongdoing.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:43.360
In return, God demanded that members of the
Foundation only worshipped him and no other

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.200
divine entities.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:51.920
“I, the LORD, am a jealous God, visiting
the iniquity of the fathers upon the children

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:58.560
unto the third and fourth generation of them
that hate me” was written in the contract.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:04.320
Finally, the agreement between the O5 Council
and God was that they would work together.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.800
The Foundation and the counterparty would
be equal partners when it came to the containment

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.520
of SCPs and anomalies.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:16.560
Of all the strange and unexplained phenomena
that the SCP Foundation encounters on a regular

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:21.680
basis, it hardly comes as much of a surprise
that they’ve got a direct line to the big

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:23.280
guy upstairs.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.760
Or at least one who purports to be.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:30.240
Still, the fact that the O5 Council have a
business arrangement with an ultra powerful

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:35.440
deity like being, and express written permission
to use his Blind Spot where no person can

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:39.040
die or age, is hardly a comforting thought.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:44.240
At least the SCP Foundation only ever uses
its power for good… right?

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:51.680
Now go check out “SCP-001 - Which is the
Real 001?” and “SCP-001 - When Day Breaks”

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:54.960
for more SCP-001 action!

